title: Allogeneic stem cell transplantation in nodal TFH lymphoma
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

* ''Role:'' Potentially curative through graft-versus-lymphoma activity; preferred for eligible patients with relapsed/refractory nodal T-follicular helper (TFH) lymphoma, including after failed autologous transplant. Not routine consolidation in first complete remission.
* ''Timing:'' Refer early and initiate donor search. Aim for disease control; refractory disease worsens outcomes but does not preclude benefit.
* ''Survival:'' In a retrospective CIBMTR cohort of 249 patients with angioimmunoblastic T-cell lymphoma (a nodal TFH subtype), 4-year overall survival was ''56%'', progression-free survival ''47%'', and relapse/progression ''21%''.
* ''Non-relapse mortality:'' ''19% at 1 year; 30% at 4 years''. Balance curative potential against GVHD, infection, and organ toxicity; performance status and comorbidities guide selection.
* ''Caveat:'' These historical, selected transplant recipients do not represent every nodal TFH subtype.

Sources: [[CIBMTR 2019|https://doi.org/10.1186/s13045-018-0696-z]]; [[EBMT 2025|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40610175/]]; NCCN T-Cell Lymphomas v2.2026, PTCL-7/MS-24–25.
